# User Story v6

Workbook: `docs/specs/User_Story_v6_20_11_2026.xlsx` (20 Nov 2026). Indexes: `docs/specs/meal-service-modules.md`.

| Role | Stories |
|---|---|
| User | USR-01–USR-50 |
| Admin | ADM-01–ADM-21 |
| Dietitian | DIT-01–DIT-16 |
| Kitchen | KIT-01–KIT-15 |
| Delivery | DEL-01–DEL-13, DEL-15–DEL-17 (no DEL-14) |

- Implement the workbook text. When you need acceptance criteria, read that story's rows only.
- Do not open `docs/specs/*.pdf` or any retired handoff. DIT-17 is not in v6.
- Quoted UI strings go in `frontend/src/user/data/messages.ts` (staff copy under `frontend/src/admin`).
- The user (account) and the meal recipient are different people on a family account. One meal recipient per account.
- Record cross-module conflicts. Do not invent staff behavior.
- Passed / Failed / Total rows are not requirements. Status is in `docs/implementation-traceability.md` and `docs/implementation-traceability-staff.md`. Do not mark a story complete without a mapped test.
- Screen grouping follows `docs/specs/millers-law-guideline.md` and does not change acceptance criteria.
